        "original_id": "98fd7a4d-1011-5a82-94c9-5ecbc65d349a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ben Elton, Andrew Lloyd Webber, Glenn Slater, Frederick Forsyth, Summer Strallen\n- Works: The Young Ones, Blackadder, We Will Rock You, Love Never Dies, The Phantom of the Opera, The Sound of Music\n- Topics: Alternative comedy, musicals, theatre\n\nFacts:\n- Ben Elton was born on 3 May 1959 and is an English comedian, author, playwright, actor, and director.\n- In the 1980s, Ben Elton was part of London's alternative comedy movement.\n- In the 1980s, Ben Elton became a writer on the series The Young Ones and Blackadder while continuing as a stand-up comedian on stage and television.\n- In 2002, Ben Elton wrote the musical We Will Rock You.\n- Love Never Dies is a romantic musical with music by Andrew Lloyd Webber, lyrics by Glenn Slater, and a book by Andrew Lloyd Webber, Ben Elton, Frederick Forsyth, and Glenn Slater.\n- In 2010, Ben Elton wrote the musical Love Never Dies, which is the sequel to The Phantom of the Opera.\n- Ben Elton has published 15 novels.\n- Summer Strallen played Meg Giry in the West End production of Love Never Dies.\n- Summer Strallen played Maria von Trapp in Andrew Lloyd Webber's revival of The Sound of Music at the London Palladium.",
